WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
<i>This show contains scenes that some viewers may
find disturbing. Viewer discretion is advised.</i>

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.900
Excuse me for interrupting, but 
I'm gonna announce it one more time.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.710
The winner of the third game, 
Friendly Hide-and-Seek, is...

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.870
<b>Group C</b>

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.870
<b>Third Game  Friendly Hide-and-Seek</b>

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.870
<b>Cleared</b>

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.870
Group C! The game is over!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.160
Huh?! How?!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.210
We found their hider first, didn't we?

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:36.140
That's true. Group K did find 
the other team's hider first.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.600
So we're the winners, then.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:44.190
Oh, but that's not the only way
 for a team to win, right?

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.810
<i>N-No way!</i>

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.060
Sorry, guys.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.210
I pushed the give-up button.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.180
Friendship

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:14.340
thief

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:14.340
parent and child crooks

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>Before the End of the Third Game</b>

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.800
It can't get any worse.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.230
<b>Episode 11: Do You Really Have Nothing You Care About?</b>

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:28.830
<b>Episode 11: Do You Really Have Nothing You Care About?</b>

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.830
This is the worst thing 
that could have happened.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:36.300
Hey, Hyakutaro, nobody
 else is nearby, right?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.040
Y-Yeah, I think they all went 
looking for Mikasa.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.660
Okay. We should get started, then.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:44.390
Huh?

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:50.210
The truth is, the moment you switched teams,
 our victory became certain.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.360
I really didn't want to have 
to win this way, is all.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:02.900
This really is the worst thing that 
could have happened, Hyakutaro.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.530
<b></b>Incoming call

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.530
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi (Group C)

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:07.500
Hello?

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.330
<i>This is Katagiri Yuichi.</i>

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.630
<i>I don't have much time, 
so I'll get straight to the point.</i>

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.090
<i>Please push the give-up button.</i>

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.450
Are you screwing with me?

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.590
There's no way I'll push it.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.430
In that case, I'm going to punch 
Hyakutaro until you push it.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.300
Y-You're bluffing!

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.770
<i>I'm sure you'd like to believe that, 
but I've run out of options.</i>

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.660
<i>First punch. Here we go.</i>

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>And the second!</i>

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.260
<i>Third!</i>

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.070
<i>Fourth!</i>

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.460
<i>Fifth!</i>

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.070
Stop! It won't work!

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.230
You're crazy if you think you can 
break me with a bluff like this.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.150
<i>I'll keep going then. Sixth!</i>

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.500
I-If you really were punching him,
 then why isn't Hyakutaro making any sound?

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:04.330
<i>Yeah, that surprised me, too. 
He sure is tough.</i>

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.710
<i>Do you want to hear his voice?</i>

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.770
<i>I'm f-fine, Captain.</i>

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.260
<i>It's a bluff, just like you said.</i>

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.190
<i>Don't push the button!</i>

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.750
<i>T-The waver in his voice...</i>

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.900
<i>Is he really...</i>

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.020
What do you mean, "monster"?

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:29.990
Katagiri Yuichi... This guy is the devil.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.160
<i>Seventh!</i>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.390
Sorry, Hyakutaro!

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:38.040
It won't be long before Kei 
and the others find their hider.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.030
Just hold on until then.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.360
<i>This is a breeze. A breeze.</i>

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.130
<i>I mean, he isn't really hitting me anyway.</i>

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.810
<i>Here I go. Eighth!</i>

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.600
Damn it!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.570
<i>At this rate, it is starting to look 
like he can really take it.</i>

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.650
<i>Well, in that case,</i>

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.660
<i>I'll have to break something 
that can't be fixed.</i>

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.610
W-What's that supposed to mean?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.230
I heard about you guys.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:07.120
You're all on the same 
basketball team, right?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.950
Hyakutaro-kun told me about it.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:13.180
In the last tournament, 
he kept missing shots

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.830
and ended up getting you injured.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.430
He practiced his shots 
like crazy after that.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.210
<i>What the hell are you planning?!</i>

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.510
Please push the button. If you don't...

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.760
<b></b>I'll break Hyakutaro's finger

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.010
I'll break Hyakutaro's finger.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.890
<i>You can't make shots in basketball 
without a delicate touch, right?</i>

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:37.310
<i>Once a finger is broken, even if 
you recover and rehabilitate it...</i>

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.190
Y-You piece of shit!

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.130
<i>You have ten seconds.</i>

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.320
<i>Ten, nine, eight,</i>

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.950
W-Wait a minute!

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.440
<i>seven, six, five, four...</i>

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.140
<i>Hey! What the hell—</i>

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.060
<i>I'm gagging you so that 
you can't bite your tongue.</i>

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.920
<i>Three, two, one...</i>

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.090
<i>Maybe he didn't really... break it?</i>

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.460
<i>No, I'll never forget that sound.</i>

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.260
<i>It sounded just like when it happened to me.</i>

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.870
I'm sorry, Hyakutaro!

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.190
<i>Which finger shall I do next?</i>

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.140
You can't be serious...

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.220
<i>Of course I can.</i>

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:23.060
<i>I'll keep breaking fingers until 
you push the button. Really.</i>

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:27.710
Stop it! You scum!

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:30.040
<i>No, you're the scum.</i>

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.580
<i>I mean, you were the one who
 started all this, weren't you?</i>

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.990
What did you... say?

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.120
<i>You're the reason your team is playing the 
Tomodachi Game in the first place.</i>

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.420
<i>Your debt is what started it.</i>

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.960
<b></b>Your debt is what started it

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.590
So you knew.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.840
Well, yeah.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.260
It seemed like a taboo topic in Group K.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:57.270
But none of the three I talked 
to knew whose debt it was.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:01.780
At first, I thought the one with
 the debt was the youngest, Kei,

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:05.440
but then I realized the power 
dynamics went the other way.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:10.410
Basically, it made sense to assume 
the debt belonged to the captain.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.570
I learned about you from Hyakutaro.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.450
You're willing to put your 
life on the line for people.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:21.450
But you also can't handle it 
if you're responsible

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:25.210
for someone else getting hurt.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.910
My family business was drowning in debt.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:33.700
It got so bad, I was going to have to 
quit high school and start working.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:39.100
But I wanted to play one 
last tournament with everyone,

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.870
and then Kei said

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.900
he'd help me pay it off, on the condition 
that I obeyed his every word.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.500
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you, guys.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.690
This is all my fault.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.650
But even though that's true,

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.540
I'll never forgive you for what you did!

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.770
I will never...

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.710
ever forgive...

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.130
a cowardly piece of shit like you!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.340
Stop! That's enough!

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.630
Why are you stopping me?!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.930
It's really not a big deal!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.510
B-But your finger...

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.760
He broke your finger!

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.940
B-But that sound I heard was clearly...

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.940
M-My god, did you...

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.530
You broke your <i>own</i> finger?!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.910
We had reasons why we 
absolutely couldn't lose.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.990
That's why I chose to—

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.820
No, that isn't it.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.580
I just couldn't think of any better way.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:51.340
I guess I really am a
 cowardly piece of shit.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.840
Hyakutaro, why didn't you tell me?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:02.350
Well, he said he'd let you hit him
 as much as he hit me.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.000
We've lost this match.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Group C</b>

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Third Game    Friendly Hide-and-Seek</b>

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Cleared</b>

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Two Million Yen Award Obtained</b>

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.280
Oh, no we haven't.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.740
There's no way I'm settling for that.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.700
<i>We</i> lost? Speak for yourself.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:23.800
<i>You're</i> the one who lost, blockhead.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.220
Come on, Kei!

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:30.250
Shut the hell up! The rest of you 
held me back just as much as he did.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.830
My plan was <i>perfect</i>.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:37.090
But still, you were <i>completely</i> useless.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:38.520
Th—

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:39.540
Whap!

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.010
What are you doing, Banri-niichan?!

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.390
Banri... niichan?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.430
I'm not his real brother.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.450
We grew up together. I was like 
the typical neighborhood "older brother."

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.310
I had no idea.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:52.970
Give it up, Kei.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:56.530
Your strategy didn't account 
for this situation, so you lost.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:00.320
And Juzo made the right 
choice in pressing the button.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.530
Why's that?

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.040
Because if he had thrown 
Hyakutaro under the bus,

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.080
I would have lost all respect for him.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:11.540
That makes sense. I guess I would have, too.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.830
And then we would have lost 
the next game no matter what.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.860
Kei.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:22.220
One day, "I have lost" 
will be a great asset.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.330
Yeah, what's that line from?

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.850
It's from my bible.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.520
But what are we going to do now? 
We still have the debt.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:34.110
We might never be able to 
see each other again after this.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:37.630
I'll have them pass all 
of the remaining debt to me.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:38.340
Bye-bye!

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:43.450
And I'll ask them to make sure you guys 
at least don't get split up.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.790
Captain...

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.050
Are you really okay with that?

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:50.670
What about your dream for us 
to play in one last tournament?

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.390
It's all right.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.760
We did get to play one last, 
great match together.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:58.570
Oh.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:03.160
U-Um, Yuichi-kun?

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.570
I was wondering, did you know about me?

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:09.750
Yeah. You work for the management, right?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.890
I figured it out.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.020
O-Of course you did.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.280
Huh?!

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.440
For the weak and insecure girl 
you were trying to play,

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.610
you followed my difficult 
instructions a little <i>too </i>perfectly.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.200
I see.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.990
And since I knew you were 
with the management,

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.970
I pushed you off that cliff without guilt.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.040
Rude!

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:32.060
Then, your reaction when
 I betrayed you was also...

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:37.420
It was all an act to make Group K think they
 were winning, so they'd leave me behind.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:42.500
You had me eating out of 
the palm of your hand, huh?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.180
Pass this message along to your bosses:

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.800
"I will absolutely crush all of you."

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.770
You bet!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.510
Can you stand?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:56.810
Yeah. Ouch!

00:11:56.810 --> 00:12:01.740
Yuichi, you said you were 
a cowardly piece of shit,

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.820
but I don't think you are.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:11.170
You don't always have 
the nicest ideas, but take a look.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.400
You didn't destroy their 
friendship after all.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:20.510
I don't care what anyone else says. 
I know you're a good person.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.190
Thanks, Tenji.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:27.930
<i>But... if he was any slower 
pushing that button,</i>

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.040
<i>I really might have broken 
Hyakutaro's finger.</i>

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:37.150
<i>The old me would have 
broken it without flinching.</i>

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:43.280
<i>If you knew about that side of me, 
would you still tell me I'm a good person?</i>

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.280
<i>Would you still think of me as a friend?</i>

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.700
Congratulations on clearing the third game!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:55.540
There's a little time left before the fourth 
game begins, so I'll let you leave for a while.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:00.500
Of course, don't tell anyone about this, 
and don't try to run away.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:05.930
If you try anything like that, 
the others will be in real trouble.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.680
We're back.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:13.430
Yeah. Let's go and find Sawaragi right now.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.090
At this hour, we might be 
able to catch Shiho-chan alone.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.430
She was always the first one at school.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.320
Always the stalker.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.320
Let's go and find out the truth.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.660
K-Kokorogi?

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:31.580
Yuichi?!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.740
<b>YOU COCKROACH</b>

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.740
<b></b>family of crooks

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.740
<b>Don't ever come back
 to this school!!</b>

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.870
What the hell happened here?

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b>FILTHY THIEF!</b>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b>DIE CRIMINAL</b>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b></b>die

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b>Give it back,
 asshole</b>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b></b>We'll find you

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b>you piece of shit</b>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b>GIVE THE MONEY BACK THIEF</b>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.870
<b></b>you suck

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.840
Shiho-chan and Shibe-kun have disappeared!

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.090
<b>One Week Earlier</b>

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:44.350
Since you three are exempt 
from the third game,

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:46.590
I'll let you go home temporarily.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.710
But you can't talk to anyone about the game, 
and you'd better not run away.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:53.090
Why would you even think we'd do that?

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.730
There's too much going on 
that we don't understand,

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.480
and we won't run or hide 
until we do understand.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:02.360
That's my Shiho-sama, always 
ready with the cool one-liners.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.940
In that case, I'll tell you 
something nice before you go.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:09.820
Right now, Group C's total debt amount is

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.260
10.8 million yen.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.130
10.8 million?

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.210
Shiho, what's wrong?

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.580
N-Nothing at all.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:22.480
We shouldn't listen to 
what Manabu says, anyway.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:23.650
Why not?

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:28.970
Because we all know it's all just lies 
intended to poison our friendship.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.100
Well, believe me or don't, that's up to you.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:36.730
But incidentally, Yuichi-kun and
 Tenji-kun both already know about it.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.850
Oh. They must have asked...

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:45.690
Yuichi, there's no mistake, then.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.290
Shiho-chan's secret got out and she ran.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.370
Secret?

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:55.080
I d-don't really understand, but there was 
a reason why Shiho-chan disappeared.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:55.080
<b>Don't ever come back
 to this school!!</b>

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.080
<b>YOU COCKROACH</b>

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:55.080
<b></b>family of crooks

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.820
No matter what, try to act natural.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.710
If we seem shaky and weird, 
people might start asking questions.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:01.940
Y-Yeah.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.050
Mm-hmm.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.090
Morning, everyone!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.270
Hey, Sawaragi-san.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:10.380
Hanamiya-san?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.930
As class vice president, 
I'll get right to the point.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.600
You were the one who stole 
the class trip funds, weren't you?

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.810
Don't people usually save 
money like that in an account?

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.750
The other classes said they did.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:28.570
Sensei said that you insisted 
on collecting it in cash.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.140
No matter how you look at it, 
you seem really suspicious.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.990
Calm down, you guys!

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.870
Shiho isn't the thief.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.250
Because the thief is—

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.240
Don't, Shibe!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.680
It has to do with that game. 
You shouldn't say too much.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.170
O-Oh, right.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:49.170
You should also know, Shibe, 
that we think you're an accomplice.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:53.460
You've got to be kidding. 
Do you know how rich I am?

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.220
Huh?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.750
Come on, two million 
isn't enough to cry over.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.600
All right, about that two mil...

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:02.440
I'll lend you the whole amount!

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.000
That's a bad move.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.590
Yeah, that would have pissed everyone off.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.690
No, that's not what I mean.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.490
Kokorogi,

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.820
did some kind of big 
incident happen after that?

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.830
H-How did you know?

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.280
Well, two days after that,

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:21.450
Shibe-kun's dad got arrested.

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:21.450
<b>Breaking</b>

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:21.450
<b>Sitting City Council Member Shibe Masakazu Arrested!</b>

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.100
It seems like the police 
found out about all the stuff

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.420
that was exposed in the second game.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.730
Then does that mean...

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.440
Yeah, Shibe talked.

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:34.220
He told his dad about the Tomodachi Game.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:39.320
Not even Shibe could get 
two million yen without an adult's help.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:41.830
Shibe-kun came to school the next day

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:44.770
and apologized to everyone, 
saying he couldn't get the money,

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.560
but then everyone started 
really bullying him.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.280
Shiho-chan tried to stand up for him, 
but then she stopped coming to school, too.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:51.270
<b>YOU COCKROACH</b>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:51.270
<b>family of crooks</b>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:51.270
<b>Die!</b>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:51.270
<b>Don't ever come back 
to this school!!</b>

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.600
Y-You guys!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.240
Why are you at school?

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.200
I thought you'd be with Shibe.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.330
What are you talking about?

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.580
Something's going down at Shibe's place.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.580
Isn't this Shibe Masakazu's home?

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.190
The council member they arrested?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.080
There's a body?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:07.840
Suicide?

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.010
I heard it was murder.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:09.870
Murder?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:10.430
Who did it?

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:11.590
It was...

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.280
Shibe's dad was...

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:14.670
Murdered?

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.300
Hey, they're coming out.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.900
Shibe!

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:23.330
W-Why is this happening?

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.030
Shibe! Shibe!

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.650
What the hell's going on?!

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:28.810
Yuichi? Tenji?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.180
No! This isn't right. It isn't!

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:33.250
I wanted Shiho to—

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.360
You'd better not say too much.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.780
<i>That man...</i>

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.990
It's Shiho-chan's father.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.040
Tenji-kun? Why are you—

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.080
M-My father... Were you the one—

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.460
Calm down, Tenji! There's no proof yet!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.710
Um, we're friends of Shibe Makoto-kun,

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.590
and we wanted to know what happened.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.090
Is that right?

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:01.120
Sorry, I can't talk about it in detail.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.310
The police are sworn 
to confidentiality. And...

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.560
You don't want to get involved in this.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.990
If there's anyone or 
anything you care about,

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:12.490
don't stick your nose 
into others' business.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:15.120
You don't want to lose what's 
precious to you, do you?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.030
That basically means nothing to me.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:24.340
I don't have family or anything else 
to care about, really.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.200
So your threats aren't going to work.

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:31.830
What I mean is that if you want to stop me, 
you'll have to come straight at me.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.300
What is going on, anyway?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.220
For now, all we can do 
is find out more about Shibe.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:42.170
Yuichi, do you think Shiho-chan 
is tied up in this, too?

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:43.880
W-What do you mean?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.580
Kokorogi-san.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.940
W-What do you mean? 
What did Shibe-kun do?!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.230
What does Shiho-chan have to do with it?!

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.310
Well, we don't really know all the—

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:56.150
You're lying! You're both hiding 
something from me, aren't you?!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.230
You were acting weird this morning, too!

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:02.590
And after all that in the second game,
 you trust each other now?!

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.450
And Yuichi's hurt!

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.100
Come on, tell me! What are you hiding?

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.120
We can't...

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.160
Why the hell would we tell you?

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:13.710
As soon as the second game ended,

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.050
I was through with you.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:19.210
You looked at me like 
I was a monster, didn't you?

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:23.180
You didn't say a word to me 
before I went to the third game.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.260
That's not what I'd call a friend.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:31.020
I was just scared, because they 
said you were a murderer.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:35.320
But I waited! I waited 
to find out the truth.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.640
Even though I was scared, 
I waited for you both to come back.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.950
That's only because 
Sawaragi told you to, right?

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.120
You only do what people tell you to do.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:49.080
Quit talking to me like I owe you something!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:52.840
Kokorogi, let me make this 
crystal clear for you.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:56.920
People like you, who can't decide 
a single damn thing on their own...

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:59.460
There's nothing in the world I hate more!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.680
Get lost. I'm done with you.

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:07.980
What about the Tomodachi Game? 
Won't you be in trouble without me?

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.220
Nah, you're useless.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:15.100
I guess you didn't notice how much 
of a burden you are for everyone else.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.230
O-Of course I knew...

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:21.780
I could tell that from the start!

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:26.250
That's why I always did 
what you guys told me.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:29.420
I didn't want to be in the way!

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.760
Yeah, and I'm telling you that 
you're in the way right now.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:36.710
Kokorogi, you're a stranger to us now.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.840
Was that the right thing to do?

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.120
It's not about right or wrong. 
Lives are on the line.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.760
We should leave Kokorogi out of it.

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:52.970
If we tell the management that we'll take 
on Kokorogi's debt, they shouldn't complain.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.920
Unknown caller?

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:02.570
Hello?

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:06.550
<i>Sorry to surprise you, but we're going to 
start a special Tomodachi Game right now.</i>

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:15.290
<b></b>Unknown Caller

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:15.290
<b></b>In Call

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.210
<i>Katagiri Yuichi-kun is there too, right?</i>

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.870
<i>Is it true that threats don't work on you</i>

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.730
<i>because there's nothing 
and nobody you care about?</i>

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.120
What are you trying to say?

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:17.500
Kokorogi?!

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:20.370
<i>The game rules are super simple, man.</i>

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.750
<i>All you have to do is choose between 
two options: show up, or don't.</i>

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:26.890
<i>If you do show up, you'll 
have a really terrible time.</i>

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:31.300
<i>If you don't, Kokorogi Yutori will 
have a little bit of a terrible time.</i>

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.440
<i>The game you two are playing this time is</i>

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.690
<b></b>The Weak Win Game

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:35.980
<i>The Weak Win Game, got it?</i>

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.560
The weak win?

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.810
<b>100% Damage</b>

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.810
<b>100% Damage</b>

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:40.440
<i>For example, if two different people 
suffer the exact same amount of pain,</i>

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.580
<i>one with self control won't scream.</i>

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:45.570
<b></b>Weak Person

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:45.570
<b>Strong Person</b>

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:45.950
<i>A weak person, however, 
will immediately start screaming.</i>

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.820
<b>Strong Person</b>

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.380
<i>You'd think the strong person 
is superior, right?</i>

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:49.200
<i>But you know,</i>

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:54.450
<b></b>Weak Person

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:52.350
<i>in our world, people will say the person 
who screamed is a "poor thing"</i>

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.450
<i>and go easy on them.</i>

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:57.470
<i>That's outrageous, isn't it?</i>

00:21:57.470 --> 00:22:01.540
<i>If self control is a disadvantage in this world, 
it's almost as if the weak win.</i>

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.540
<b>Absolutely Refuse</b>

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.540
Stop!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.540
<b>I protest!</b>

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:06.140
<i>Yuichi-kun, if you're showing up, 
come to the designated location alone.</i>

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:10.900
<i>If you bring anyone else, 
you'll never see Kokorogi Yutori again.</i>

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:13.700
<i>And if you </i>do<i> show, 
I promise you'll have</i>

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:16.720
<i>a </i>much<i> worse time than Kokorogi Yutori.</i>

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:21.990
<i>Basically, if you don't show up,
 you'll end up objectively less injured...</i>

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:23.330
<i>but what do you wanna do?</i>

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:26.740
If you do anything to Kokorogi,

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:28.820
I will kill you.

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:32.510
Are you going, Yuichi?

00:22:32.510 --> 00:22:36.450
We got Kokorogi caught up 
in this thing, so I think I have to.

00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:38.750
On top of that, this one...

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:45.300
is going to be different 
from the other games.

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:49.840
<b>NEXT: What's Most Important to Me Is...</b>
